# Example E1 — justified-clean (the happy path, the vertical slice)
#
# Witnesses: the smallest end-to-end pipeline — one leaf-backed controlled_experiment
# scheme instance, all three mandatory critical questions discharged by pattern-matching
# leaves, no attacks. The single support argument is `in` under grounded semantics, so the
# headline claim aggregates to `justified` (spec §8 priority: some support `in`).
#
# This is E1 of the M4a coverage matrix (docs/worked-examples-plan.md §3): status = justified,
# attacks = none. It is the "leaf → scheme → support term → compile → grounded → aggregate"
# walk with every corner clean, so a failure here localizes to the pipeline, not the calculus.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact resnet_c01 at sha256:e1e1...
policy empirical-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim ------------------------------------------------------------------------

claim c1
  nl      = "Method M improves accuracy on distribution D"
  formal  = improves(M, accuracy, D)
  binding = { author = alice, audit-status = reviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The principal premise of the controlled_experiment scheme (reconstructed implicitly by the
# elaborator from `by controlled_experiment(M, accuracy, D, exp_1)`, spec §5).
leaf e1 : reports(exp_1, effect(M, accuracy, D, positive))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [evidence/table_1.csv#row=mean]

# The three mandatory critical questions, each discharged by a leaf whose proposition matches
# the policy's answer pattern exactly (randomization=randomized(Exp), adequate_power=powered(Exp),
# external_validity=generalizes(M,Q,D)).
leaf e2 : randomized(exp_1)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = user
  refs       = [paper.pdf#sec=4.1]

leaf e3 : powered(exp_1)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = user
  refs       = [paper.pdf#sec=4.1]

leaf e4 : generalizes(M, accuracy, D)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = user
  refs       = [paper.pdf#sec=5]

# --- The support argument ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# A complete controlled_experiment instance: all three mandatory CQs discharged, no open holes,
# no attacks. Its conclusion improves(M, accuracy, D) ≡ c1's formal, so it supports c1.
arg a1 : supports(c1) by controlled_experiment(M, accuracy, D, exp_1)
  discharge randomization     with e2
  discharge adequate_power    with e3
  discharge external_validity with e4

status c1

# ==============================================================================================
# EXPECTED VERDICT (golden oracle) — verified by test/WorkedExamplesSpec.hs
# ==============================================================================================
# Compiled AF: one argument, unattacked.
#   a1  -> in    (LIn; no attackers, so it is in the grounded extension)
# Claim status:
#   c1  -> justified   (its only support a1 is `in`; spec §8 aggregation)
#
# Teaching point: the happy path is boring on purpose — every critical question is answered by a
# leaf that matches its policy pattern, so nothing attacks and nothing is left open. This is the
# baseline the E2 gap and the E3 defeats deviate from.
